AllRADecoder: the noise buttons call a hook when one is set (a3-core's SPEAKERS page).

Applied by cmake/A3IemNodes.cmake at configure time to a copy of AllRADecoder/Source in the
build tree (patch -p1 from that Source directory); third_party/IEMPluginSuite stays clean at
its pin. The window hosts IEM's AllRADecoder editor on a processor that never gets audio:
playNoiseBurst (a row's Noise button) and playAmbisonicNoiseBurst (the same with Alt) call
a3NoiseHook / a3AmbisonicNoiseHook when set, and the window posts the burst to the engine,
which plays IEM's NoiseBurst / AmbisonicNoiseBurst in that zone (src/iem-nodes/ZoneNoise.cpp).
Unset, IEM's own behaviour is unchanged. And (2026-10-31) the 3D view's OpenGL clear colour is a member,
a3Ground, IEM's grey by default: the window sets its card's colour (a component effect never reaches an OpenGL
clear). Configure fails if this no longer applies.

--- a/PluginProcessor.h
+++ b/PluginProcessor.h
@@ -97,6 +97,10 @@
 
     void playNoiseBurst (const int channel);
     void playAmbisonicNoiseBurst (const float azimuth, const float elevation);
+    // a3 patch (a3-core patches/iem/AllRADecoder-noise-hook.patch): when set, the noise buttons call
+    // these instead of the processor's own bursts; the window has no audio, the engine plays them.
+    std::function<void (int)> a3NoiseHook;
+    std::function<void (float, float)> a3AmbisonicNoiseHook;
     void addRandomPoint();
     void addImaginaryLoudspeakerBelow();
     void clearLoudspeakers();
--- a/PluginProcessor.cpp
+++ b/PluginProcessor.cpp
@@ -562,12 +562,16 @@
 
 void AllRADecoderAudioProcessor::playNoiseBurst (const int channel)
 {
+    if (a3NoiseHook != nullptr)
+        return a3NoiseHook (channel);
     noiseBurst.setChannel (channel);
 }
 
 void AllRADecoderAudioProcessor::playAmbisonicNoiseBurst (const float azimuthInDegrees,
                                                           const float elevationInDegrees)
 {
+    if (a3AmbisonicNoiseHook != nullptr)
+        return a3AmbisonicNoiseHook (azimuthInDegrees, elevationInDegrees);
     auto dec = decoder.getCurrentDecoder();
     if (dec != nullptr)
     {
